---
import Layout from "@/layouts/Layout.astro"
import SectionContainer from "@/components/SectionContainer.astro"
import CaseHeader from "@/components/CaseHeader.astro"
import {
  TALLER_WEEKS,
  TALLER_TOTALS,
  EGRESO_RUBROS,
} from "@/data/taller-operacion.js"

const maxIngreso = Math.max(...TALLER_WEEKS.map((w) => w.ingresos))
const bs = (n: number) => `Bs. ${n.toLocaleString("en-US")}`
const RUBROS_EN: Record<string, string> = {
  "Filamentos / Plastic 27": "Filament / Plastic 27",
  "Sueldos y salarios": "Wages and salaries",
  "Alquileres": "Rent",
  "Insumos y herramientas": "Supplies and tools",
  "Servicios básicos": "Utilities",
  "Otros egresos": "Other expenses",
}
const pct = (monto: number) => Math.round((monto / TALLER_TOTALS.egresos) * 100)
const filamentoPct = pct(EGRESO_RUBROS[0].monto)
const filamentoSueldosPct = pct(EGRESO_RUBROS[0].monto + EGRESO_RUBROS[1].monto)
---

<Layout
  title="Workshop operations analysis | Diego Sarmiento"
  description="Data analyst case: 12 weeks of workshop operations, SQL, KPIs and business recommendations."
>
  <main class="px-4 py-24">
    <SectionContainer>
      <CaseHeader
        kicker="Data analyst · case study"
        title="Where the money gets stuck in a workshop"
        summary="Question: if orders keep growing, why does the margin not follow and why do uncollected parts keep piling up? A 12-week practice sample in the same domain as Vehimac (these are not the client's accounting figures)."
      />

      <div class="mt-10 grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-4">
        <div class="rounded-xl border border-gray-200 bg-white p-4 dark:border-gray-800 dark:bg-gray-900">
          <p class="text-sm text-gray-500 dark:text-gray-400">Revenue (12 wk)</p>
          <p class="mt-1 text-2xl font-semibold text-gray-800 dark:text-white">{bs(TALLER_TOTALS.ingresos)}</p>
        </div>
        <div class="rounded-xl border border-gray-200 bg-white p-4 dark:border-gray-800 dark:bg-gray-900">
          <p class="text-sm text-gray-500 dark:text-gray-400">Margin</p>
          <p class="mt-1 text-2xl font-semibold text-gray-800 dark:text-white">{TALLER_TOTALS.margenPct}%</p>
        </div>
        <div class="rounded-xl border border-gray-200 bg-white p-4 dark:border-gray-800 dark:bg-gray-900">
          <p class="text-sm text-gray-500 dark:text-gray-400">Quote → work order conversion</p>
          <p class="mt-1 text-2xl font-semibold text-gray-800 dark:text-white">{TALLER_TOTALS.conversion}%</p>
        </div>
        <div class="rounded-xl border border-gray-200 bg-white p-4 dark:border-gray-800 dark:bg-gray-900">
          <p class="text-sm text-gray-500 dark:text-gray-400">Uncollected parts (W12)</p>
          <p class="mt-1 text-2xl font-semibold text-yellow-600 dark:text-yellow-200">{TALLER_TOTALS.sinRecoger}</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <section class="mt-14 space-y-4 text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-gray-800 dark:text-white">Approach</h2>
        <ol class="list-decimal space-y-2 pl-5">
          <li>Define KPIs with the business: revenue on delivery, expenses by category, finished order ≠ paid order.</li>
          <li>Clean: a finished work order is not revenue until it is <code>entregado</code> (delivered).</li>
          <li>Aggregate by week and by category (SQL below).</li>
          <li>Cross quote conversion with the backlog of uncollected parts.</li>
        </ol>
      </section>

      <section class="mt-12">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-gray-800 dark:text-white">Revenue vs expenses by week</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 mb-6 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400">
          Revenue grows towards the end of the quarter; so do expenses,
          mostly filament and wages. The margin is squeezed in W3, W6 and W9.
        </p>
        <div class="space-y-3">
          {
            TALLER_WEEKS.map((w) => (
              <div>
                <div class="mb-1 flex justify-between text-xs text-gray-500 dark:text-gray-400">
                  <span>{w.semana.replace("S", "W")}</span>
                  <span>{bs(w.ingresos)} / {bs(w.egresos)}</span>
                </div>
                <div class="flex h-3 overflow-hidden rounded bg-gray-100 dark:bg-gray-800">
                  <div
                    class="h-full bg-yellow-500 dark:bg-yellow-300"
                    style={`width:${Math.round((w.ingresos / maxIngreso) * 100)}%`}
                  />
                </div>
                <div class="mt-1 flex h-2 overflow-hidden rounded bg-gray-100 dark:bg-gray-800">
                  <div
                    class="h-full bg-gray-400 dark:bg-gray-500"
                    style={`width:${Math.round((w.egresos / maxIngreso) * 100)}%`}
                  />
                </div>
              </div>
            ))
          }
        </div>
        <p class="mt-3 text-xs text-gray-500 dark:text-gray-400">
          Yellow bar: revenue. Grey bar: expenses. Scaled to the highest weekly revenue in the sample.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="mt-12">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-gray-800 dark:text-white">SQL used</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400">
          Queries written against the Vehimac schema (<code>finances</code>,
          <code>work_orders</code>, <code>proformas</code>).
        </p>
        <pre class="mt-4 overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-gray-200 bg-gray-50 p-4 text-sm text-gray-800 dark:border-gray-800 dark:bg-gray-900 dark:text-gray-200"><code>{`-- 1) Cash by week. The source is finances: wages and rent are not
--    tied to a work order, so the query does not start from work_orders.
SELECT
  date_trunc('week', f.date)::date AS semana,
  SUM(f.amount) FILTER (WHERE f.type = 'ingreso') AS ingresos,
  SUM(f.amount) FILTER (WHERE f.type = 'gasto')   AS egresos
FROM finances f
GROUP BY 1
ORDER BY 1;

-- 2) Expenses by category and their share of the total.
SELECT
  f.category AS rubro,
  SUM(f.amount) AS monto,
  ROUND(100.0 * SUM(f.amount) / SUM(SUM(f.amount)) OVER ()) AS share_pct
FROM finances f
WHERE f.type = 'gasto'
GROUP BY 1
ORDER BY 2 DESC;

-- 3) Uncollected parts: finished work orders not yet delivered.
--    It is a point-in-time snapshot, recorded once a week.
SELECT
  COUNT(*) AS sin_recoger,
  MIN(wo.updated_at)::date AS la_mas_antigua
FROM work_orders wo
WHERE wo.status = 'terminado';

-- 4) Quote → work order conversion: a converted quote stores its order.
SELECT
  COUNT(*) AS proformas,
  COUNT(p.work_order_id) AS ots,
  ROUND(100.0 * COUNT(p.work_order_id) / NULLIF(COUNT(*), 0)) AS conversion_pct
FROM proformas p
WHERE p.created_at >= now() - interval '12 weeks';`}</code></pre>
      </section>

      <section class="mt-12">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-gray-800 dark:text-white">Expenses by category</h2>
        <div class="mt-4 overflow-x-auto">
          <table class="w-full text-left text-sm text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300">
            <thead>
              <tr class="border-b border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-700">
                <th class="py-2 font-medium">Category</th>
                <th class="py-2 font-medium">Amount</th>
                <th class="py-2 font-medium">Share</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              {
                EGRESO_RUBROS.map((row) => (
                  <tr class="border-b border-gray-100 dark:border-gray-800">
                    <td class="py-2">{RUBROS_EN[row.rubro] ?? row.rubro}</td>
                    <td class="py-2">{bs(row.monto)}</td>
                    <td class="py-2">{pct(row.monto)}%</td>
                  </tr>
                ))
              }
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="mt-12 space-y-4 text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-gray-800 dark:text-white">Findings</h2>
        <ul class="list-disc space-y-2 pl-5">
          <li>
            Average ticket of {bs(TALLER_TOTALS.ticket)} across {TALLER_TOTALS.entregadas} deliveries.
          </li>
          <li>
            Uncollected parts go from 4 to 12: finished work that is not
            cash yet.
          </li>
          <li>
            Quote → work order conversion at {TALLER_TOTALS.conversion}%:
            {100 - TALLER_TOTALS.conversion}% of what gets quoted never reaches
            production.
          </li>
          <li>
            Filament + wages are ~{filamentoSueldosPct}% of expenses. The W6 and W9 peaks coincide
            with more quotes and fewer closed work orders.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="mt-12 space-y-4 text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-gray-800 dark:text-white">Recommendations</h2>
        <ol class="list-decimal space-y-3 pl-5">
          <li>
            Automatic WhatsApp message 48 h after a work order reaches
            <em>finished</em>, and again after 7 days. Goal: bring uncollected
            parts from 12 to under 6 within a month.
          </li>
          <li>
            Do not open a new work order when the customer already has 2
            uncollected parts (unless they pay an advance). It frees capacity
            and cash.
          </li>
          <li>
            Review the W6 and W9 quotes (many quotes, low conversion):
            filament price vs. what was quoted.
          </li>
          <li>
            Buy filament against accepted work orders, not “just in case”
            stock. It is {filamentoPct}% of expenses.
          </li>
          <li>
            Read the income statement by week first, not by month: the three
            margin dips disappear in the monthly aggregate.
          </li>
        </ol>
      </section>

      <p class="mt-12 text-sm text-gray-500 dark:text-gray-400">
        Limitation: a practice sample to show the method (question → SQL
        → finding → action). In a real role I would run the same queries on
        the Vehimac Postgres with the shop's data.
      </p>
    </SectionContainer>
  </main>
</Layout>
